Before C++11, C++ had many different initialization styles:

```cpp
int x = 10;
int y(20);
std::vector<int> v;
v.push_back(1);
v.push_back(2);
```

C++11 introduced brace initialization:

```cpp
int x{10};
std::vector<int> v{1, 2, 3};
```

Main idea:

```text
Use one consistent syntax to initialize objects.
```

---

